Patch 25: honour the dry pass in tx_type_rd, as its sibling path already does.

Standalone, against anchor 5d628d8. Supersedes patch 0024, which was a
confirmed no-op in CTC and should be dropped.

MEASURED LOCALLY, PAIRED, 3 REPS: +6.86%, +9.16%, +5.00% -- mean +7.01%,
sd 2.08%, all three the same sign. 192x128, 4 frames, cpu-used=4, alternating
two saved binaries. The bitstream changes (md5 eeebfc00 vs ab4e2d32), so there
is a real quality cost that only CTC can price. A small clip is not a CTC
result and the magnitude will move at 4K; what this establishes is that the
patch fires and that the effect is large enough to be worth an arm.

THE FINDING. A callgrind profile of this encoder at cpu-used=4 puts trellis
quantisation at about 47% of all instructions retired -- more than partition
search, mode search and the loop filters combined -- and
av2/encoder/trellis_quant.c contains no speed-feature references at all. It
runs at full strength at every preset and every stage of the search.

The two-pass dry pass is supposed to avoid exactly this.
choose_tx_size_type_from_rd says so in as many words:

    // Dry pass: skip trellis (no RDOQ) - light quant only.
    const int skip_trellis = x->apply_dry_pass_shortcuts ? 1 : 0;

But tx_type_rd, a few hundred lines away in the same file, had:

    const int skip_trellis = 0;

hard-coded. So the trellis ran at full strength there even during the dry pass,
whose entire purpose is to rank partition shapes cheaply. tx_type_rd is reached
from try_tx_block_no_split -- once per transform block per transform partition
candidate -- which makes it one of the densest trellis call sites in the
encoder.

This is a consistency fix, not a new heuristic. It applies the policy the dry
pass already declares, at a site that was not honouring it. The wet pass is
untouched and still runs the full trellis for the real coding decision.

WHY THE EARLIER ATTEMPTS MISSED IT. Patch 0023 reduced the dry pass's mode and
precision caps and returned +6.15% at +0.58% BD-rate, ratio ~10.6 against a bar
of 25 -- it bought speed by degrading the shape ranking. Patch 0024 targeted
the transform-type pruning helpers and was bit-identical in CTC, because those
sites need num_allowed > 2 and are rarely reached. Neither touched
quantisation, which is where the time actually is. This patch does, and it does
so by removing work the code already intended to skip rather than by ranking
less carefully.

-DAVM_TX_TYPE_RD_DRY_TRELLIS=1 restores the hard-coded 0 exactly.

diff --git a/av2/encoder/tx_search.c b/av2/encoder/tx_search.c
index 593fd92..3bfc1c7 100644
--- a/av2/encoder/tx_search.c
+++ b/av2/encoder/tx_search.c
@@ -3012,7 +3012,39 @@ static AVM_INLINE void tx_type_rd(const AV2_COMP *cpi, MACROBLOCK *x,
   av2_subtract_txb(x, AVM_PLANE_Y, plane_bsize, blk_col, blk_row, tx_size,
                    cpi->common.width, cpi->common.height, DCT_DCT);
   RD_STATS this_rd_stats;
+  // Honour the dry pass here, as the sibling path already does.
+  //
+  // A callgrind profile of this encoder at cpu-used=4 puts trellis
+  // quantisation at ~47% of all instructions retired -- larger than partition
+  // search, mode search and the loop filters combined -- and
+  // av2/encoder/trellis_quant.c contains no speed-feature references at all.
+  //
+  // The two-pass dry pass is supposed to avoid it. choose_tx_size_type_from_rd
+  // says so explicitly:
+  //
+  //     // Dry pass: skip trellis (no RDOQ) - light quant only.
+  //     const int skip_trellis = x->apply_dry_pass_shortcuts ? 1 : 0;
+  //
+  // This function had a hard-coded 0 instead, so the trellis ran at full
+  // strength here even during the dry pass. tx_type_rd is called from
+  // try_tx_block_no_split, i.e. once per transform block per transform
+  // partition candidate, which makes it one of the densest trellis call sites
+  // in the encoder -- and the dry pass, whose whole purpose is to rank
+  // partition shapes cheaply, was paying for it.
+  //
+  // This is a consistency fix rather than a new heuristic: it applies the
+  // policy the dry pass already declares, at a site that was not honouring it.
+  // The wet pass is unaffected and still runs the full trellis.
+  //
+  // -DAVM_TX_TYPE_RD_DRY_TRELLIS=1 restores the hard-coded 0.
+#ifndef AVM_TX_TYPE_RD_DRY_TRELLIS
+#define AVM_TX_TYPE_RD_DRY_TRELLIS 0
+#endif
+#if AVM_TX_TYPE_RD_DRY_TRELLIS
   const int skip_trellis = 0;
+#else
+  const int skip_trellis = x->apply_dry_pass_shortcuts ? 1 : 0;
+#endif
   int dummy = 0;
   search_tx_type(cpi, x, 0, block, blk_row, blk_col, plane_bsize, tx_size,
                  &dummy, txb_ctx, ftxs_mode, skip_trellis, ref_rdcost,
